{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/deployment/providers","title":"Deployment providers","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"deployment-providers","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Deployment providers"}]},{"t":"callout","tone":"warning","caption":"Experimental","children":[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The provider contract is not settled: the method signatures below, the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"capability list and the plan shape can still change between minor versions. A"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"provider written today may need a small update to keep up."}]}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A provider is the integration that builds, publishes or provisions a platform."},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"It is never a runtime of CraftTS, and never a dependency of the application"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"bundle: the CLI owns the manifest and delegates every mutation to a provider"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"package installed separately."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A provider implements this contract:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"export","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"type","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"CraftDeploymentProvider","kind":"type"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"readonly","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"name"},{"text":":","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"string","kind":"type"},{"text":";","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"readonly","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"capabilities"},{"text":":","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"readonly","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"CraftDeploymentCapability","kind":"type"},{"text":"[];","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"check","kind":"function"},{"text":"?","kind":"keyword"},{"